<title>SWEDEN: Swedish Riksbank board meeting ends, no changes.</title>
<headline>Swedish Riksbank board meeting ends, no changes.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's central bank, the Riksbank, on Thursday held a board meeting which ended with no rate changes announced.</p>
<p>The Riksbank on Tuesday lowered its key repo rate by 25 basis points to 4.10 percent. The repo is the central rate in the bank's interest rate corridor.</p>
<p>Its other key rates, the deposit and lending rates, currently stand at 3.75 percent and 5.25 percent respectively.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
